<title>SOUTH AFRICA: NO DECISION ON REPAYMENT OF S.AFRICA MAIZE LEVIES.</title>
<headline>NO DECISION ON REPAYMENT OF S.AFRICA MAIZE LEVIES.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's Maize Advisory Committee said on Tuesday that consensus could not be reached at a meeting last Thursday on repaying levies paid by farmers into the Maize Board's stabilisation fund.</p>
<p>The committee's acting chairman Leon du Plessis said in a statement the repayment had been proposed by the National Maize Producers Organisation.</p>
<p>The country's state-owned Maize Board is being closed down following legislation last year that outlaws statutory control boards.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
